# Intent: the screen can no longer stay dim with no way back (owner 2026-11-16, standing next to the unit: the screen went dim and stayed dim, tapping the face did not undim it, and the quick settings swipe seemed to do nothing because its panel opened at the same dim level). Root cause, in four links: (1) the host dims the screen by calling the stock tool self.screen.set_brightness (rest stage asleep: 5, night rule: 15); (2) that stock tool SAVED the value, so the dim level became the level the unit boots into and RestoreBrightness returns to; (3) the host sets a level again only when its rest stage or night edge changes, and its night sync stops at a face tool this firmware does not have, so a unit that restarted while dimmed (the restart guard, a reset, a power loss) came back dim and stayed dim; (4) nothing on the unit itself woke the screen: no touch, touch bar, shake, tilt or wake word touched the backlight. Fix: (a) the host's brightness is live only (mcp_server.cc), and the saved level is the person's (the quick settings slider; the Backlight keeps its own copy, saved_brightness, so a wake never reads flash from a task with a stack in external RAM); (b) maipai_screen_wake(): a touch on the glass, a strong touch or swipe on the touch bar, a shake, a tilt or roll, or the wake word puts a dimmed screen back to the saved level at once and tells the host with a head_touch event (strong, tap, screen=1) so a host that put the unit to sleep wakes; (c) a press that only woke the screen starts no listen and toggles no mute, vision or quiet (the same claim the clock face uses); (d) with the hub link down for 60 s a dimmed screen returns by itself (no host is left to do it); (e) Backlight::SetBrightness no longer drops a request for the level a move in progress had just left (it compared only the live level, so the screen finished the move at the dim target), and the saved level is written even when the screen already shows it; (f) the AXP2101 supply register 0x90 is read with TryReadRegs before the screen is switched on or off: ReadReg returns 0 after three failed tries (patch R02) and a read-modify-write from that 0 would switch every other supply in the register off. New tool self.screen.get_level (saved and live); in a bench build self.screen.bench_touch presses the glass through the same function the touch chip reader calls. The pure rule is maipai_screen_core.h (host/tests/firmware/screen_core_test.c).
# Placement: unit (the screen, the touch and the backlight are the unit's; a unit must come back from a dim with the host off)
# Upstream: xiaozhi-esp32 main/boards/common/backlight.{h,cc}, main/mcp_server.cc, main/application.cc; m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/{stackchan.cc,hal_bridge.cc,stackchan_display.cc}, hal/hal_imu.cpp, hal/hal_mcp.cpp (MIT); new hal/maipai_screen.{h,cc} and maipai_screen_core.h (MIT)
# Check after a flash: self.screen.get_level answers saved and live; self.screen.set_brightness 5 then a touch on the glass (a finger, or self.screen.bench_touch in a bench build) restores live to saved within a second and the log says "screen was dim (5, saved N): restored on touch"; the host's brightness commands never change saved (read it before and after); a restart while dimmed boots at saved; a touch that wakes a dimmed screen does not toggle mute, vision or quiet.
